  "description": "Privately held United States berry marketer headquartered in Watsonville, California, active across all four berries -- blueberries and strawberries have real, dedicated evidence in this dataset; raspberries and blackberries are documented at the company-wide level (Mexico sourcing, Dutch harvest coverage) but do not yet have berry-specific evidence of their own. It breeds proprietary blueberry varieties under the 'DrisBlue...' denomination series and proprietary strawberry varieties under a closed-genetics program, does not sell its plants, and grows through a network of independent licensed growers. Also a member of the consortium that took Costa Group private in February 2024. Its closed-genetics strawberry program has been in patent-infringement litigation against California Berry Cultivars (founded by former UC Davis breeder Douglas Shaw) since 2023; CBC won summary judgment in district court in 2025 and Driscoll's has appealed.",
